 ze pool across three tracks: the main Kaggle competition on the ARC-AGI-2 
 static reasoning benchmark\, a track on ARC-AGI-3 interactive agent reason
 ing (second milestone 30 September 2026)\, and a paper prize for research 
 that advances understanding of ARC-AGI performance. Milestone prizes run U
 SD 25\,000 / 10\,000 / 2\,500. Open to individuals and teams worldwide\, e
 ntirely online via Kaggle. Winning entries must be open-sourced under perm
 issive licenses to collect prizes. Main submission deadline 2 November 202
 6\, paper track 8 November 2026\; results announced 4 December 2026.\n\nOr
 ganisation: ARC Prize Foundation\nLocation: Online (Kaggle)\, worldwide\nA
 ward: USD 2\,000\,000 total prize pool across three tracks (ARC-AGI-2\, AR
 C-AGI-3 agents\, and a paper prize)\; milestone prizes include USD 25\,000
