UID:emaf-2027-call-for-entries@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260925T222405Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261215
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261216
SUMMARY:Deadline: EMAF 2027: Call for Entries\, Film / Installation / Expan
 ded
DESCRIPTION:The European Media Art Festival (EMAF) in Osnabrueck invites su
 bmissions for its 2027 edition in three sections: Film (experimental films
  of all lengths and any theme)\, Installation (installative\, interactive\
 , spatial or sculptural media art works) and Expanded (performances\, live
  events or workshops). WHAT YOU GET: all films selected for the Internatio
 nal Selection are equal winners of the EMAF Award with EUR 400 prize money
  each\; films in the Features section (over 60 minutes) receive a EUR 250 
 screening fee\; curated programmes pay EUR 80-250 depending on length\; in
 stallations and expanded projects receive a EUR 500 fee with production co
 sts paid by the festival. Selected artists are invited to the festival wit
 h free accreditation\, three hotel nights (potentially longer if setting u
 p is required) and a contribution to travel costs. RULES: maximum 2 works 
 per artist\; only works completed in 2026 or 2027 are eligible\; no premie
 re status required\; works entered at previous editions will not be recons
 idered. Films up to 60 minutes are viewed for the International Selection\
 , films over 60 minutes for Features. Installation entries should relate t
 o the 2027 festival theme of the archive (as an instrument of knowledge pr
 oduction\, a site of critical intervention and a space for alternative vis
 ions of the future)\; Installation and Expanded entries must include a com
 prehensive description\, tech rider\, cost calculation and visual material
 s. Non-English-language works must have English subtitles for the selectio
 n screening. Submit digitally via the EMAF registration portal (no DVDs or
  physical media). Selection decisions are emailed from mid-March 2027. DEA
 DLINE: the call closes as soon as 2\,200 entries have been received\, or a
 t the latest on 15 December 2026\, so submit early. No entry fee.\n\nOrgan
 isation: European Media Art Festival (EMAF)\nLocation: Osnabrueck\, German
 y. Open worldwide\; selected artists are invited to the festival with free
  accreditation\, three hotel nights and a contribution to travel costs.\nA
 ward: All films in the International Selection are equal winners of the EM
 AF Award and receive EUR 400 each. Screening fees: EUR 250 for Features\, 
 EUR 80-250 for curated programmes depending on length\, EUR 500 for instal
 lations and expanded projects\; production costs for installations and exp
 anded projects are paid by the festival. Selected artists get free accredi
 tation\, three hotel nights (longer if setup requires) and a travel cost c
 ontribution. No entry fee.\nDuration: Festival in Osnabrueck\, spring 2027
 \; screening prints must arrive by 1 April 2027\n\nMore: https://emaf.film
 chief.com/entry-forms?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
URL:https://emaf.filmchief.com/entry-forms?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Osnabrueck\, Germany. Open worldwide\; selected artists are invite
 d to the festival with free accreditation\, three hotel nights and a contr
 ibution to travel costs.
END:VEVENT
