DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261016
SUMMARY:Deadline: LOEWE FOUNDATION: Craft Prize 2027
DESCRIPTION:The 10th edition of the LOEWE FOUNDATION Craft Prize is open fo
 r registration until 15 October 2026. Established in 2016\, the prize rewa
 rds works combining technical excellence\, artistic quality and innovation
  in craft. WHAT YOU GET: the winner receives EUR 50\,000\, and shortlisted
  works are shown in an exhibition in Europe in spring 2027. DISCIPLINES: t
 extiles are explicitly listed among the eligible craft disciplines\, along
 side ceramics\, woodwork\, metalwork and other applied arts\, which makes 
 the prize a home for e-textile and material-innovation work with a craft d
 imension. ELIGIBILITY: entries must be original one-of-a-kind works made e
 ntirely or partly by hand\, created within the last five years\, and not p
 reviously awarded a prize\; applicants must be professionals at least 18 y
 ears old\, and individuals and collectives of all nationalities may apply.
  DEADLINE: registration closes 15 October 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nOrganisati
 on: LOEWE FOUNDATION\nLocation: Worldwide\; shortlist exhibition in Europe
  in spring 2027. Open to professional artisans aged 18 or over\, individua
 ls or collectives\, all nationalities.\nAward: EUR 50\,000 for the winning
  entry. No application fee.\nDuration: One-off prize\; shortlisted works s
 hown in an exhibition in Europe in spring 2027.\n\nMore: https://craftpriz
 e.loewe.com/en/craftprize2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://craftprize.loewe.com/en/craftprize2027?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Worldwide\; shortlist exhibition in Europe in spring 2027. Open to
  professional artisans aged 18 or over\, individuals or collectives\, all 
 nationalities.
